    "question": {
      ":question/id": "60b1552e-a565-551e-a09c-c978389eed9b",
      ":question/problem": "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ n\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $p\u22a5q$, find the value of $n.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $p\u22a5q$ ($p$ and $q$ are perpendicular) if and only if $p\\cdot q=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 6+n\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-18-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ -18-4n & =0 \\\\ -18 & =4n \\\\ n & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
