      ":question/problem": "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}2{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g\u22a5h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $g\u22a5h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8{r}^{2}-4{r}^{2}-6 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
