      ":question/problem": "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}3{r}^{2} \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3{r}^{2} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g\u22a5h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $g\u22a5h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 3{r}^{2}+(-2)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12{r}^{2}-9{r}^{2}-8 \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 3{r}^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ 3{r}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}.$",
